A community skin is its catalog entry (catalog/skins/<id>.json), the recipes its
implementations name, with the glyph masks and other art they hold, and the scripts under
scripts/skins/ that generate those recipes, the source of its art (each names its skin and
carries the SPDX identifier CC-BY-SA-4.0). The entry's "licence" field states CC-BY-SA-4.0 and
its "authors" field names who made it; a recipe a skin names is named by no feature and no other
skin.

Everything else in this repository, including feature recipes and the glyph masks they hold,
is licensed under the MIT licence in LICENSE.
